  "paid_answers": {
    "history": {
      "answer": "Tyrconnel (GSQ site 43836, 3.0 km ene of thornborough) is recorded by the Geological Survey of Queensland as abandoned mine, gold size band small, 0.5 - 5 t. Reported production: 1,819.3 kg gold, about 58,492 oz troy (converted here; the survey records 1,819.3 kg) (to 1988, Tyrconnel, per GSQ MINOCC 2017 (Total_Ores_Prod, SITE_NO 43836)); 50,888 tonnes ore (to 1988, Tyrconnel, per GSQ MINOCC 2017 (Total_Ores_Prod, SITE_NO 43836)). GSQ MINOCC 2017 also lists 1 dated Production row (gold: 1,819.3 kg to 1988); see production. Ownership and tenure: Bell per GSQ MINOCC 2017 (Tenure, SITE_NO 43836); Gold Copper Exploration Ltd (1987 to 1989) per GSQ MINOCC 2017 (Explorer, SITE_NO 43836, row 1); Wmc Ltd (1985 to 1988) per GSQ MINOCC 2017 (Explorer, SITE_NO 43836, row 2); Stannary Mining Pty Ltd (1982 to 1987) per GSQ MINOCC 2017 (Explorer, SITE_NO 43836, row 3). GSQ MINOCC 2017 lists 6 company reports for this site: CR 12774, CR 13470, CR 15336, CR 15760, CR 16303, CR 16609. Not found: closure: no closure year or reason in the sources indexed for this site.",
