    "survey": {
      "answer": "Tyrconnel (Geological Survey of Queensland site 43836) is recorded as an abandoned mine on the Rumula 1:100,000 sheet (3.0 km ene of thornborough.), at -16.9343, 145.0352, located to within 100 m. The survey classes its gold as small, 0.5-5 t, and also records tungsten (very small). Within 5 km it records 74 other historical workings, 74 of them with gold; other commodities nearby: antimony, silver, tungsten. The record gives a size band, not production figures, and holds no owners or closure dates.",
